    "body": "### Problem\n\nThe `foldcolumn` currently has configurable characters for the beginning of an open fold (`foldopen`), the middle of an open fold (`foldsep`), and a closed fold (`foldclose`), but no character for the end of an open fold.\n\nThis makes it difficult to render an unambiguous fold outline, especially with nested folds. A configuration such as `foldopen:╭,foldsep:│,foldend:╰,foldclose:▶` would provide a consistent visual grammar:\n\n```text\n╭  fold starts\n│  fold continues\n╰  fold ends\n▶  fold is closed\n```\n\nNeovim 0.12 added `foldinner`, which improves narrow fold columns, but it does not indicate where an open fold ends.\n\n### Expected behavior\n\nAdd a `foldend` item to `'fillchars'`, with a default such as `╰` (and `-` as the single-byte fallback). It should be used in the fold column on the last visible line of an open fold, at the corresponding fold level. Nested folds that end on the same line should be able to show the marker at each ending level.\n\nThe marker should not replace `foldclose` for closed folds, and `foldopen` should take precedence for a one-line fold that starts and ends on the same line.\n\nThis is backwards-compatible: the new item would simply fall back to its default when omitted.\n\nreleted: https://github.com/gh-liu/fold_line.nvim",
